finding: The new optional mapped properties accept explicit undefined under this project's strict tsconfig (exactOptionalPropertyTypes is not enabled), but World.add treats every non-number as an array and dereferences lanes[0]. A typechecked call such as world.add(eid, { x: f32 }, { x: undefined }) throws TypeError and leaves the component attached; retrying with values then follows the already-attached no-op path. Optional starting values assembled from optional game configuration therefore have a typed-valid crash path. Handle undefined as omitted (preserving defaults), or reject it in the public type under the supported compiler settings, and cover it. Independently reproduced the throw and remaining membership; scratch tsc produced no diagnostic for scalar: undefined while correctly rejecting the four existing negative type controls.
